electron-antineutrino-symbol-7dd3ed9a.symmetry_origin:
The existence of the electron antineutrino, $\bar{
u}_e$, is intrinsically linked to fundamental symmetries in particle physics, particularly the conservation of lepton number and CPT symmetry. In processes like beta decay, the emission of an electron, $e^-$, necessitates the simultaneous emission of an electron antineutrino, $\bar{
u}_e$, to conserve the total electron lepton number. Its antiparticle nature is a direct consequence of CPT symmetry, which postulates that physical laws are invariant under combined charge conjugation ($C$), parity transformation ($P$), and time reversal ($T$).
